From: Uke Linux project <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: arm the Uke Bluetooth wake IRQ after suspend

Uke s2idle immediately wakes on the Bluetooth RX wake IRQ. Disabling only
that wake source allows the RTC to resume the tablet after the alarm delay.
OEM Uke and same-SoC Nord 4 GENI suspend code arm RX wake after resources
are disabled. Use the standard reverse-order dedicated wake IRQ API for
the exact Uke Bluetooth child, retaining normal ordering for other ports.

The host fixture checks selection, OF lifetime and the existing error path.
Physical suspend and Bluetooth wake validation are still required.

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index 88f9ba0..813d9c3 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1917,9 +1917,18 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto error;
 
 	if (port->wakeup_irq > 0) {
+		struct device_node *bt;
+
 		device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev, true);
-		ret = dev_pm_set_dedicated_wake_irq(&pdev->dev,
-						port->wakeup_irq);
+		bt = of_get_compatible_child(pdev->dev.of_node, "xiaomi,uke-wcn6750-bt");
+		/* Uke's RX wake line must be armed after the UART resources turn off. */
+		if (bt)
+			ret = dev_pm_set_dedicated_wake_irq_reverse(&pdev->dev,
+							port->wakeup_irq);
+		else
+			ret = dev_pm_set_dedicated_wake_irq(&pdev->dev,
+							port->wakeup_irq);
+		of_node_put(bt);
 		if (ret) {
 			device_init_wakeup(&pdev->dev, false);
 			ida_free(&port_ida, uport->line);
